Description: Provides programmatic access, local caching, spatial subsetting,
    temporal aggregation, anomaly computation, and validation metrics for the
    Peruvian Interpolated data of SENAMHI's Climatological and hydrological
    Observations (PISCO) developed by SENAMHI DHI-SEH. Supports the complete
    family of PISCO products: precipitation (PISCOp v3.0, PISCOp_h),
    temperature (PISCOt v1.2 daily, monthly, and climatology), reference
    evapotranspiration (PISCOeo_pm), rainfall erosivity (PISCO_reed v1.0),
    and monthly streamflow with basin and river networks (PISCO_HyM GR2M and
    ARNOVIC) hosted on Figshare and HydroShare. Includes optimized workflows
    for basin-scale extraction, seasonal aggregations, and spatial raster and
    vector processing based on 'terra' and 'sf'.
